d development', 'frontend development', 'api integration'], 'uid': 'freelancer:40684645', 'country': 'UN', 'language': 'en', 'tags': ['PHP', 'JavaScript', 'Website Design', 'SEO', 'WordPress', 'HTML', 'Web Development', 'Backend Development', 'Frontend Development', 'API Integration']}, {'title': 'Elegant Real Estate Website Build', 'description': 'The task is to build a neat, clean and fully responsive real-estate website that feels classic and elegant while remaining highly interactive. I already have the brand direction; what I need is the complete design-to-deployment workflow handled so the site loads quickly, guides visitors smoothly through each page, and converts casual browsers into qualified leads.\n\nAnimations  \nTo create a polished, conversational experience the front-end must include:  \n• Page transitions that feel seamless, not jarring  \n• Subtle hover effects on cards, buttons and thumbnails  \n• Lightweight loading animations that reassure users while content fetches  \n\nCore functionality  \n• Property listings that I can add, edit and archive from an admin area  \n• Robust search and filter options (price, location, bedrooms, etc.) so buyers find the right home fast  \n• Secure user login and registration to let visitors save favourites and schedule viewings  \n\nStyle & UX  \nThe design language should be classic and elegant—think harmonious typography, a reserved colour palette, generous white space and refined micro-interactions. The layout has to stay consistent across desktop, tablet and mobile. Accessibility and SEO best practices are non-negotiable.\n\nTech stack & workflow  \nFeel free to propose the framework or CMS you believe delivers the smoothest performance; React, Vue, Next.js, Laravel or a well-optimised WordPress build are all acceptable as long as the end result meets the speed and security benchmarks. Source control via Git and a staging link for iterative reviews are required.\n\nDeliverables  \n1. Fully deployed website on